  "major": "film-media-production-bfa-nyc-9399d1d4",
  "major_name": "Film and Media Production",
  "degree": "BFA",
  "campus": "New York",
  "college": "College of Arts, Media and Design",
  "overview_text": "The Bachelor of Fine Arts in Film and Media Production is designed to equip students with the essential artistic, technical, and intellectual skills to excel in the highly competitive film, television, and digital media industries. The program seeks to develop creative storytellers who are not only proficient in the tools of media production but are also critical thinkers, innovators, and responsible global citizens. Individualized attention and hands-on training using state-of-the-art equipment, combined with a strong liberal arts foundation, position students to create meaningful, socially engaged media projects. Students are encouraged to immerse themselves in the industry by taking internships in television, film, radio, emerging technology, and media production companies. This comprehensive education in film and media emphasizes both creative expression and professional development, preparing graduates to thrive in various roles within the ever-evolving media landscape. This program is currently only available to former Marymount Manhattan College students who are eligible for continued enrollment at Northeastern University. This program includes required courses that will be taught on ground at the Northeastern New York City campus.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences Requirements\nAll undergraduate students enrolled in programs at the New York campus are required to fulfill\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences requirements\n.\nRequired Courses\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nFilm and Media Production Courses\nCOMM 1122\nStorytelling Across Media\n4\nMSCR 1100\nFilm 101\n4\nMSCR 2105\nSound Production for Digital Media\n4\nMSCR 2111\nTelevision Field Production\n4\nMSCR 2121\nTelevision Studio Production\n4\nMSCR 2255\nNew Media Workshop\n4\nMSCR 3437\nMedia and Identity\n4\nMSCR 3450\nDirecting Video\n4\nMSCR 4991\nResearch\n4\nCapstone\nCOMM 4755\nProduction Capstone\n4\nFirst-Year Writing Requirement\nENGW 1111\nFirst-Year Writing\n4\nMajor Electives\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete four of the following:\n16\nARTD 3480\nVideo: Sound and Image\nCOMM 1210\nPersuasion and Rhetoric\nCOMM 1412\nSocial Movement Communication\nCOMM 2534\nGroup Communication\nCOMM 2912\nSpecial Topics in Communication Studies\nCOMM 3912\nSpecial Topics in Communication Studies\nJRNL 3370\nPodcast and Radio Journalism\nJRNL 5314\nVideo News Reporting and Producing\nMSCR 2170\nProducing for the Entertainment Industry\nMSCR 2300\nTelevision: Text and Context\nMSCR 2325\nGlobal Media\nMSCR 3150\nDigital Editing for TV\nMSCR 3389\nScreenwriting: Short Film\nMSCR 3420\nDigital Media Culture\nMSCR 3973\nSpecial Topics in Media and Screen Studies\nMSCR 5300\nMedia and Technology Ethics\nMajor Credit Requirement\n56 semester hours required in the major\nGeneral Electives\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete remaining program required hours and NUpath requirements via general electives.\nOptional Co-op\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nSuccessful completion of EXED 2000 is required for participation in co-op.\nEXED 2000\nProfessional Development for Co-op\n1\nCOOP 3945\nCo-op Work Experience\n0\nor\nCOOP 3946\nCo-op Work Experience--Half Time\nor\nCOOP 3947\nCo-op Work Experience Abroad--Half Time\nor\nCOOP 3948\nCo-op Work Experience Abroad\nProgram Requirement\n128 total semester hours required",
